<p>
  <b>mhs</b> gives the non-singular half-space Green's functions for
  triangular dislocation elements. Following Cortez, the point force
  is replaced by a smooth blob of width &epsilon;
  so a fault has a finite width and stress is defined on the fault itself, where
  classical dislocation theory returns a value ordinary integration does not
  define. The free surface is carried by the Mindlin image terms, not by a
  meshed boundary. The library builds the on-fault interaction matrix used in
  static stress transfer and rate-and-state and earthquake-cycle models.  Note
  this is WIP developed by Claude based on:
  <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.15601">arxiv.org/abs/2609.15601</a>.
</p>
